                        <field name="dc_description">The name of this machine often causes confusion because it is not the well-known company founder Elipalet Remington and the inventor Christopher Latham Sholes, but their sons, who were also active in the industry. After confronting E. Remington & Sons, the two changed the company name to Fay-Sholes Typewriter Company in 1901.<br/>
Special features of this machine: moving lever basket, black hard rubber buttons, keyboard locking at the line end and with the ribbon coil expired.<br/>
Ident-No.: Fabriknr.: 1959 <br/>
<br/>
Martin, Ernst. The typewriter and her developmental history. Aachen, Germany: Peter Basten, 1949 (Deutsches Technikmuseum) </field>
